{
  "unit": {
    "id": "es-a2-u04",
    "title": "Irregular preterite",
    "subtitle": "The most common irregular past-tense verbs",
    "level": "A2",
    "order": 4,
    "xp_reward": 20
  },
  "grammar": {
    "title": "Past tense, but off the beaten path",
    "intro": "You already know how to form the regular <b>preterite</b> (the finished past: <i>hablé, comí, viví</i>). But the verbs you'll use most — <b>ser, ir, estar, tener, hacer</b> — are irregular. The good news: they share one special set of endings and take <b>no accent marks</b>. Learn these five and you can talk about almost anything you did.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "tag": "ser / ir",
        "heading": "ser and ir: same forms, context decides",
        "body": "Here's a Spanish gift: <b>ser</b> (to be) and <b>ir</b> (to go) share the <b>exact same</b> preterite. The sentence tells you which one it is:",
        "conj": [
          [
            "yo",
            "fui"
          ],
          [
            "tú",
            "fuiste"
          ],
          [
            "él/ella",
            "fue"
          ],
          [
            "nosotros",
            "fuimos"
          ],
          [
            "vosotros",
            "fuisteis"
          ],
          [
            "ellos",
            "fueron"
          ]
        ],
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "<b>Fui</b> al cine ayer.",
            "en": "I went to the cinema yesterday.",
            "note": "here fui = ir (to go)"
          },
          {
            "es": "La fiesta <b>fue</b> increíble.",
            "en": "The party was incredible.",
            "note": "here fue = ser (to be)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "estar / tener",
        "heading": "estar and tener: the -uv- pattern",
        "body": "Many irregulars use a special stem plus the endings <b>-e, -iste, -o, -imos, -isteis, -ieron</b> (no accents!). <b>Estar</b> → estuv-, <b>tener</b> → tuv-:",
        "conj": [
          [
            "estar → yo",
            "estuve"
          ],
          [
            "estar → él/ella",
            "estuvo"
          ],
          [
            "tener → yo",
            "tuve"
          ],
          [
            "tener → él/ella",
            "tuvo"
          ],
          [
            "tener → nosotros",
            "tuvimos"
          ],
          [
            "tener → ellos",
            "tuvieron"
          ]
        ],
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "<b>Estuve</b> en casa toda la tarde.",
            "en": "I was at home all afternoon.",
            "note": "estar → estuve"
          },
          {
            "es": "<b>Tuvimos</b> un problema.",
            "en": "We had a problem.",
            "note": "tener → tuvimos"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "hacer / poder / poner",
        "heading": "hacer, poder, poner",
        "body": "Three more high-frequency irregulars. Note that <b>hacer</b> changes the <b>c</b> to <b>z</b> in the él/ella form (<b>hizo</b>) to keep the soft sound:",
        "conj": [
          [
            "hacer → yo",
            "hice"
          ],
          [
            "hacer → tú",
            "hiciste"
          ],
          [
            "hacer → él/ella",
            "hizo"
          ],
          [
            "poder → yo",
            "pude"
          ],
          [
            "poner → yo",
            "puse"
          ]
        ],
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "Ayer <b>hice</b> la cena.",
            "en": "Yesterday I made dinner.",
            "note": "hacer → hice (no accent)"
          },
          {
            "es": "Ella <b>hizo</b> su tarea.",
            "en": "She did her homework.",
            "note": "él/ella → hizo, with z"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "takeaways": [
      "ser and ir share one preterite: fui, fuiste, fue, fuimos, fuisteis, fueron.",
      "estar → estuve, tener → tuve, poder → pude, poner → puse.",
      "hacer → hice, hiciste, hizo (the c becomes z in hizo).",
      "These irregular forms carry NO accent marks: fui, hice, tuve."
    ],
    "mistakes": [
      {
        "w": "Ayer hací la cena.",
        "r": "Ayer hice la cena.",
        "why": "Hacer is irregular here: the yo form is hice, not the regular 'hací'."
      },
      {
        "w": "Fuí al cine.",
        "r": "Fui al cine.",
        "why": "Fui carries no accent — it's a one-syllable word."
      },
      {
        "w": "Ella hació su tarea.",
        "r": "Ella hizo su tarea.",
        "why": "The él/ella form of hacer is hizo, with a z."
      }
    ]
  },
